What does this program print?

```rust
trait Greet {
    fn name(&self) -> String;
    fn hello(&self) -> String {
        format!("Hello, {}", self.name())
    }
}

struct A;
struct B;

impl Greet for A {
    fn name(&self) -> String { "Ana".into() }
}

impl Greet for B {
    fn name(&self) -> String { "Bo".into() }
    fn hello(&self) -> String { format!("Hi {}!", self.name()) }
}

fn main() {
    println!("{} / {}", A.hello(), B.hello());
}
```

Using the lesson's `Fraction` type, what do these three lines print? Write them separated by spaces.

```rust
println!("{}", Fraction::new(2, 4) + Fraction::new(1, 4));
println!("{}", Fraction::new(-3, -9));
println!("{}", Fraction::new(4, 2) * Fraction::new(1, 3));
```

